    "level": "SHORTS",
    "overview": "Although и however оба выражают contrast, но грамматически это разные инструменты.",
    "main_rule": "Although introduces subordinate clause. However is a linking adverb connecting ideas and usually needs punctuation.",
    "form": "although + clause. Sentence. However, sentence.",
    "when_why": "Хотим одну dependent clause → although. Хотим связать две самостоятельные идеи → however.",
    "examples": "Although it was expensive, we bought it. → Хотя это было дорого, мы купили это.\nIt was expensive. However, we bought it. → Это было дорого. Однако мы купили это.\nThe solution is, however, quite expensive. → Решение, однако, довольно дорогое.",
    "special_cases": "В standard concise usage не ставь however прямо после although.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ Although it was expensive, however, we bought it. → ✅ Although it was expensive, we bought it.\n❌ However it was expensive, we bought it. → ✅ Although it was expensive, we bought it.",
    "dont_confuse": "although = grammar connector inside one structure. however = linking adverb.",
    "quick_summary": "although + clause.\nhowever + separate idea/punctuation."
  },
